   758	### 4.3 Section 4: orientation typo and the omitted companion case
   759	
   760	The p. 16 sentence assigning (\widetilde a) to the right vertex and
   761	(\widetilde b) to the left is reversed.  Formula (4.1) assigns to
   762	(\widetilde a) left degrees (1,3) and lower degrees (1,2), which is the
   763	visually **left** l-block of Fig. 11(2a); it assigns to (\widetilde b)
   764	lower degrees (1,3) and right degrees (1,2), the visually **right**
   765	j-block.  The final inclusion
   766	((\widetilde b\widetilde g_2)\subset
   767	\operatorname {br}_{\widetilde a}(\widetilde b)) is well typed only with
   768	that order.  Repair: read “left (respectively right).”  **Verdict:
   769	REPAIRED[SECTION-4-a-b-REVERSAL].**
   770	
   771	With that correction, (4.2) is reproducible.  At the left vertex select a
   772	full degree-one left branch of determinant (\det L_a>1) and the full
   773	degree-one lower branch not reaching (\widetilde g_1), of determinant
   774	(\det D_a>1).  If the root lay toward (\widetilde b), these would be two
   775	non-root non-unit branches, violating [4], Lemma 3.  Thus
   776	
   777	\[
   778	\widetilde v\notin\operatorname {br}_{\widetilde a}(\widetilde b),qquad
   779	\det\operatorname {br}_{\widetilde a}(\widetilde b)=1.
